# Source layout

This page is a map of the current Neon Pairs source tree and the responsibilities of its files.

Paths here are relative to the project root. They describe authored source and configured outputs. [Module layout policy](module-layout-policy.md) explains placement decisions; this page is for finding the implementation.

## Entry and project root

`index.html` contains the document metadata, the `root` element and the development module entry `/src/main.tsx`. It declares English, a responsive viewport, the theme color `#090B14` and the title Neon Pairs. The source HTML references a module; the production HTML is assembled by Vite and the single-file plugin.

`src/main.tsx` looks up the root, throws `Missing application root.` if it is absent and renders `<Game />` under React `StrictMode`. There is no second application page or router mounted beside it. The game begins at `src/game/Game.tsx`.

The root also holds `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, four compiler configuration files, three Vite configurations and `vitest.config.ts`. `.prettierrc.json` configures formatting; `.prettierignore` and `.gitignore` identify generated or local work. The README records setup, commands, delivery, replay and the named runtime evidence.

## Game composition

`Game.tsx` calls the solo `useGame`, passes session values and controller actions into the ordinary screen, and imports `game.css`. It keeps that screen mounted while Tournament is open so the solo game state and board focus survive. The solo controller's clock is inactive until the user returns.

Its one extra coordination operation is Resume. It asks the board's imperative ref to focus the remembered card, then calls the controller's resume action. That keeps the DOM focus handoff outside the core state. `Board` is keyed by `session.generation`, so a replacement remounts the board's local state.

`game.css` defines root colors and spacing values, system typography, page geometry, global focus styling and the reserved turn-feedback area. The more specific board, control and status rules live beside their components. [CSS organization](css-organization.md) records selectors and cascade relationships.

## Core modules directly under src/game

| File                    | What a reader finds there                                                                                     |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `deck.ts`               | Supported sizes, seed bounds, board-code parser and formatter, seeded shuffle and immutable board description |
| `selection.ts`          | The closed, one-card and mismatch discriminated union                                                         |
| `game.ts`               | `GameState`, caps, creation, victory, face-up positions, activation and logical advancement                   |
| `elapsed-time.ts`       | Display formatting from elapsed milliseconds                                                                  |
| `saved-format.ts`       | Small shared JSON, object, key, integer and byte helpers                                                      |
| `snapshot-selection.ts` | Validation of matched positions and nested selection                                                          |
| `snapshot.ts`           | Snapshot version and bound, serialization and complete-state validation                                       |
| `replay.ts`             | Replay limits, structured problems, ordered actions and final state                                           |

These files use ordinary TypeScript functions and data. The core is not a React context or reducer hook. It can be imported by the session adapter and by the replay CLI without mounting the application.

`generateBoard` returns a frozen description with a frozen deck. `GameState` extends that description. Runtime progress is returned as new objects by transitions; ignored actions can return the existing object. This pattern explains why the board's memoized sets can survive clock-only updates.

## Core test files

`game.test.ts` checks card transitions and logical advancement. `completion.test.ts` finishes every supported size. `move-cap.test.ts` exercises play and records at the maximum move count. `elapsed-time.test.ts` covers the formatter and related elapsed behavior.

`deck.test.ts` checks parsing and generation. `deck-rejection.test.ts` references independently generated vectors for rejection-sampling boundaries. `game.fixture.ts` contains the example code, literal deck, pair positions, initial generator states and shared numerical specification vectors.

`snapshot.test.ts` and `snapshot-selection.test.ts` cover the outer state and nested validation. `replay.test.ts` and `replay-order.test.ts` cover replay acceptance and ordering. These files live near the rules even when a narrow regression deserves a different test filename from the principal module.

## Session directory

`session/session.ts` defines `Session`, the import notices and the pure session operations `initialSession`, `replaceGame`, `tickSession` and `activateSession`. It connects a game transition to feedback, completion state and preferences without itself calling the browser.

`session/use-game.ts` is the React controller. It reads initial preferences, creates the initial fresh board, keeps the latest session ref in step with state, exposes actions and composes the clock and saving hooks. Its options can disable saved-preference writes or pause a controller clock. Successful loads replace the game; failed loads publish notices. Exports and activations synchronize the clock first.

`session/browser-clock.ts` defines the 40ms scheduling interval and arithmetic over observed timestamps. `session/use-session-clock.ts` supplies observations, maintains visibility, schedules timeouts and removes pending work on effect cleanup. `session/browser-clock.test.ts` checks the arithmetic independently.

`session/fresh-board.ts` converts browser entropy into valid board codes, rejecting out-of-range candidates and, for a tournament schedule, duplicate full codes. `session/storage.ts` defines the preference key, version, default size, store interface, validators and best-score update. `session/use-saved-preferences.ts` obtains browser storage safely and writes changes in an effect when enabled.

`session/session.test.ts` covers state replacement, paused input, generations, repeated feedback events and completion handling. `session/storage.test.ts` uses in-memory and throwing stores to cover persistence decisions. [Session module](session-module.md) follows the exact call paths and state fields.

## Board directory

`board/Board.tsx` maps the immutable deck into cards. It derives a face-up set and a matched set, obtains the focus hook, exposes a remembered-focus method and supplies the `--grid-size` custom property. It keeps the activation callback stable while calling the latest controller action through a ref.

`board/Card.tsx` is memoized. It renders a native button, obtains its class and accessible description from `describeCard`, renders the face only when supplied and adds a matched mark for matched positions. It delegates navigation and focus to callbacks from the board.

`board/Face.tsx` converts a face design into inline SVG primitives. `board/face-design.ts` maps one of 128 face numbers to shape, marker, color, fill style, coordinates and label. `board/card-state.ts` derives a card's closed, revealed or matched description from supplied presentation data.

`board/keyboard.ts` computes arrow-navigation targets with edge stops and modifier handling. `board/use-board-focus.ts` owns the remembered position and DOM focus calls. `board/nearest-scroll.ts` remembers the viewport scroll position so focus can use nearest alignment after Chromium's automatic focus scrolling.

`board/board.css` owns the scrolling board viewport and grid tracks. `board/card.css` owns the button, concealed back, revealed/matched surfaces, corner mark and card transition. The directory's `keyboard.test.ts`, `card-state.test.ts` and `face-design.test.ts` check the numerical and descriptive helpers. Browser tests observe actual focus, artwork and scrolling.

## Controls and status

`controls/Controls.tsx` renders the grid-size select, New Game, Tournament and Restart. It reads the size options from `GRID_SIZES`. `controls/control-labels.ts` owns the solo deal and reproduction control strings.

`controls/BoardCodeForm.tsx` renders the board-code field and submit button. Its input is keyed by generation, and successful submission moves focus to the load button because the old input is replaced. An invalid submission leaves the draft available for correction.

`controls/Reproduction.tsx` holds the snapshot textarea draft in local state, renders the details disclosure and export/load buttons, and shows the load notice and conditional Resume button outside the disclosure. It uses the game code and generation passed from the parent rather than reconstructing them.

`controls/control.css` defines the common control surface. `controls/controls.css` lays out deal controls. `controls/reproduction.css` lays out the disclosure, form rows, textarea and notice region.

`status/GameStatus.tsx` renders moves, pair progress, elapsed text, optional best moves and the completion paragraph. `status/status-labels.ts` owns statistic labels. `status/status.css` styles the statistic layout and completion treatment. Solo play displays `Best`; tournament play omits it.

## Competition directory

`competition/tournament.ts` builds the four- and eight-player brackets, maps rounds to board sizes, validates names and advances results. `tournament-format.ts` encodes and validates Tournament JSON, including an active game snapshot. `tournament-storage.ts` reads and writes the feature envelope for the newest 10 finished brackets. `use-tournament.ts` coordinates form drafts, tournament actions and history. `Tournament.tsx` composes the tournament board, controls, transfer field and archive; `TournamentBracket.tsx`, `TournamentSetup.tsx` and `PastTournaments.tsx` render those focused surfaces. `tournament.css` owns their layout.

## Scripts directory

`scripts/replay.ts` is the command entry. It passes command-line arguments to `runReplay` and assigns the returned status to `process.exitCode`. `scripts/replay-cli.ts` handles one input path, caller-directory resolution, file reads, human-readable stderr failures and final snapshot output. `scripts/replay.test.ts` exercises the executable in child processes.

`scripts/source-files.ts` recursively reads ordinary files from a supplied folder and rejects links or special entries. `scripts/source-audit.test.ts` inspects packages, compiler settings, source length, unsafe constructs and selected effect boundaries. `scripts/source-conventions.test.ts` checks recognized exports/imports, yes-or-no naming, test names and environment reads.

These scripts are not imported by the application entry. Some import core functions because they are clients of the same public data behavior. That direction lets command-line replay reuse the rules without putting Node APIs into browser modules.

## Application-level test support

`tests/browser-test.ts` adapts Node tests to Playwright, manages browsers and contexts, records runtime versions, gathers page errors and provides artifact paths. `tests/artifact-server.ts` serves the built HTML over loopback. `tests/game-fixture.ts` contains public-control setup helpers, disk URLs and completion helpers.

`tests/deal-oracle.ts` independently computes a specified deal with BigInt. `tests/focus-bounds.ts`, `tests/readability.ts`, `tests/accessibility-tree.ts` and `tests/ui-snapshot.ts` provide focused measurement or comparison support. They are tools used by journeys, not application modules.

The many `.e2e.test.ts` files are grouped by the observable behavior they examine: controls, input, play, persistence, snapshots, lifecycle, clock edges, layout, motion, artwork, status, accessibility, touch and zoom. [Test policy](test-policy.md) explains the runner and evidence boundaries instead of repeating every assertion here.

## Diagnostic entries and configured outputs

`art/index.html` and `art/face-sheet.tsx` form a separate face-sheet build with `art/face-sheet.css`. It imports the real card and design definitions to render every face at a controlled size. `vite.art.config.ts` writes this entry to `.art`.

`art/session/index.html` and `art/session/session-harness.tsx` form a separate lifecycle harness. It mounts `Game` beside an unmount button. `vite.session.config.ts` writes it to `.session`. The harness exists so the browser suite can measure cleanup rather than infer it from a page navigation.

The production build writes `dist/index.html`. Local dependencies live under `node_modules`; browser downloads, temporary browser files, npm cache and test work have separate ignored directories. `test-results` holds browser runtime and journey artifacts. These directories have operational roles but are not additional application source layers.

There is no generated route tree, backend, API client, asset service or utility framework to discover beyond this map. For command ordering see [Build pipeline](build-pipeline.md); for import and runtime separation see [React boundaries](react-boundaries.md).

import { parseBoardCode } from '../deck.ts';

export type TournamentStage = 'Quarterfinal' | 'Semifinal' | 'Final';
export type TournamentPhase = 'ready' | 'playing' | 'turn-finished' | 'match-finished' | 'finished';
export interface TournamentPlayer {
  readonly seed: number;
  readonly name: string;
}
export interface TournamentResult {
  readonly seed: number;
  readonly moves: number;
  readonly elapsedMs: number;
}
export interface TournamentMatch {
  readonly round: number;
  readonly stage: TournamentStage;
  readonly boardCode: string;
  readonly players: readonly [number | null, number | null];
  readonly results: readonly [TournamentResult | null, TournamentResult | null];
  readonly winner: number | null;
}
export interface Tournament {
  readonly startedAt: number;
  readonly players: readonly TournamentPlayer[];
  readonly matches: readonly TournamentMatch[];
  readonly currentMatch: number;
  readonly turn: 0 | 1;
  readonly phase: TournamentPhase;
  readonly champion: number | null;
}

export function tournamentBoardSizes(count: number): number[] {
  return count === 4 ? [6, 6, 8] : count === 8 ? [4, 4, 4, 4, 6, 6, 8] : [];
}

export function normalizePlayerName(value: string): string {
  return value.trim().replace(/\s+/gu, ' ').normalize('NFC');
}

export function playerNamesError(names: readonly string[]): string {
  if (
    names.some((name) => {
      const length = Array.from(normalizePlayerName(name)).length;
      return length < 2 || length > 20;
    })
  )
    return 'Use 2 to 20 characters.';
  const normalized = names.map((name) => normalizePlayerName(name).toLowerCase());
  return new Set(normalized).size === normalized.length ? '' : 'Each name must be different.';
}

function openingPairings(count: number): [number, number][] {
  return count === 4
    ? [
        [1, 4],
        [2, 3],
      ]
    : [
        [1, 8],
        [4, 5],
        [3, 6],
        [2, 7],
      ];
}

export function createTournament(
  names: readonly string[],
  codes: readonly string[],
  startedAt: number,
): Tournament | null {
  if (
    (names.length !== 4 && names.length !== 8) ||
    codes.length !== tournamentBoardSizes(names.length).length ||
    !Number.isSafeInteger(startedAt) ||
    startedAt < 0
  )
    return null;
  const sizes = tournamentBoardSizes(names.length);
  if (codes.some((code, index) => parseBoardCode(code)?.size !== sizes[index])) return null;
  if (new Set(codes).size !== codes.length || playerNamesError(names)) return null;
  const players = names.map((raw, index) => ({ seed: index + 1, name: normalizePlayerName(raw) }));
  const pairings = openingPairings(names.length);
  const rounds = names.length === 4 ? [2, 1] : [4, 2, 1];
  let codeIndex = 0;
  const matches = rounds.flatMap((count, roundIndex) =>
    Array.from({ length: count }, (_, matchIndex): TournamentMatch => {
      const round = roundIndex + 1;
      const firstRound = round === 1 ? pairings[matchIndex] : undefined;
      const boardCode = codes[codeIndex++];
      if (!boardCode) throw new Error('Missing tournament deal.');
      return {
        round,
        stage:
          names.length === 8 && round === 1
            ? 'Quarterfinal'
            : round === (names.length === 4 ? 1 : 2)
              ? 'Semifinal'
              : 'Final',
        boardCode,
        players: [firstRound?.[0] ?? null, firstRound?.[1] ?? null],
        results: [null, null],
        winner: null,
      };
    }),
  );
  return {
    startedAt,
    players,
    matches,
    currentMatch: 0,
    turn: 0,
    phase: 'ready',
    champion: null,
  };
}

export function tournamentPlayer(
  tournament: Tournament,
  seed: number | null,
): TournamentPlayer | undefined {
  return seed === null ? undefined : tournament.players[seed - 1];
}

export function activeTournamentMatch(tournament: Tournament): TournamentMatch | undefined {
  return tournament.matches[tournament.currentMatch];
}

export function beginTournamentTurn(tournament: Tournament): Tournament {
  return tournament.phase === 'ready' ? { ...tournament, phase: 'playing' } : tournament;
}

export function nextTournamentTurn(tournament: Tournament): Tournament {
  return tournament.phase === 'turn-finished'
    ? { ...tournament, turn: 1, phase: 'ready' }
    : tournament;
}

import { ELAPSED_MAX_MS, MOVES_MAX } from '../game.ts';
import { activeTournamentMatch } from './tournament.ts';
import type {
  Tournament,
  TournamentMatch,
  TournamentPhase,
  TournamentResult,
} from './tournament.ts';

export function compareTournamentResults(
  first: TournamentResult,
  second: TournamentResult,
): number {
  if (first.moves !== second.moves) return first.moves < second.moves ? first.seed : second.seed;
  if (first.elapsedMs !== second.elapsedMs)
    return first.elapsedMs < second.elapsedMs ? first.seed : second.seed;
  return Math.min(first.seed, second.seed);
}

export function recordTournamentResult(
  tournament: Tournament,
  moves: number,
  elapsedMs: number,
): Tournament {
  const match = activeTournamentMatch(tournament);
  const seed = match?.players[tournament.turn];
  if (
    tournament.phase !== 'playing' ||
    !match ||
    seed === null ||
    seed === undefined ||
    !Number.isSafeInteger(moves) ||
    moves < 0 ||
    moves > MOVES_MAX ||
    !Number.isFinite(elapsedMs) ||
    elapsedMs < 0 ||
    elapsedMs > ELAPSED_MAX_MS
  )
    return tournament;
  const result: TournamentResult = { seed, moves, elapsedMs };
  const results: readonly [TournamentResult | null, TournamentResult | null] =
    tournament.turn === 0 ? [result, match.results[1]] : [match.results[0], result];
  if (tournament.turn === 0)
    return replaceCurrentMatch(tournament, { ...match, results }, 'turn-finished');
  const first = results[0];
  const second = results[1];
  if (!first || !second) return tournament;
  const winner = compareTournamentResults(first, second);
  return replaceCurrentMatch(tournament, { ...match, results, winner }, 'match-finished');
}

function replaceCurrentMatch(
  tournament: Tournament,
  match: TournamentMatch,
  phase: TournamentPhase,
): Tournament {
  return {
    ...tournament,
    phase,
    matches: tournament.matches.map((item, index) =>
      index === tournament.currentMatch ? match : item,
    ),
  };
}

export function nextTournamentMatch(tournament: Tournament): Tournament {
  if (tournament.phase !== 'match-finished') return tournament;
  const current = activeTournamentMatch(tournament);
  if (!current || current.winner === null) return tournament;
  const pending = tournament.matches.findIndex(
    (match, index) =>
      index > tournament.currentMatch &&
      match.round === current.round &&
      match.winner === null &&
      match.players[0] !== null &&
      match.players[1] !== null,
  );
  if (pending >= 0) return { ...tournament, currentMatch: pending, turn: 0, phase: 'ready' };
  const roundMatches = tournament.matches.filter((match) => match.round === current.round);
  if (!roundMatches.every((match) => match.winner !== null)) return tournament;
  const nextRound = tournament.matches.filter((match) => match.round === current.round + 1);
  if (nextRound.length === 0) return { ...tournament, phase: 'finished', champion: current.winner };
  const previousStart = tournament.matches.findIndex((match) => match.round === current.round);
  const matches = tournament.matches.map((match) => {
    if (match.round !== current.round + 1) return match;
    const matchInRound = nextRound.indexOf(match);
    const firstIndex = previousStart + matchInRound * 2;
    const first = tournament.matches[firstIndex]?.winner ?? null;
    const second = tournament.matches[firstIndex + 1]?.winner ?? null;
    return { ...match, players: [first, second] as const };
  });
  const nextIndex = matches.findIndex((match) => match.round === current.round + 1);
  return { ...tournament, matches, currentMatch: nextIndex, turn: 0, phase: 'ready' };
}

import { isJsonObject, hasExactKeys, isNonnegativeSafeInteger } from '../saved-format.ts';
import { createTournament, normalizePlayerName, playerNamesError } from './tournament.ts';
import { readTournamentMatch } from './tournament-validation-match.ts';
import {
  isTournamentProgressValid,
  isTournamentPhaseValid,
  readTournamentPhase,
} from './tournament-validation-state.ts';
import type { Tournament, TournamentMatch, TournamentPlayer } from './tournament.ts';

export function decodeTournament(value: unknown): Tournament | null {
  if (
    !isJsonObject(value) ||
    !hasExactKeys(value, [
      'startedAt',
      'players',
      'matches',
      'currentMatch',
      'turn',
      'phase',
      'champion',
    ])
  )
    return null;
  if (
    !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.startedAt) ||
    !Array.isArray(value.players) ||
    !Array.isArray(value.matches)
  )
    return null;
  const players: TournamentPlayer[] = [];
  for (const player of value.players) {
    if (
      !isJsonObject(player) ||
      !hasExactKeys(player, ['seed', 'name']) ||
      typeof player.name !== 'string' ||
      player.seed !== players.length + 1 ||
      normalizePlayerName(player.name) !== player.name
    )
      return null;
    players.push({ seed: player.seed, name: player.name });
  }
  const names = players.map((player) => player.name);
  if (playerNamesError(names)) return null;
  const count = names.length;
  if (count !== 4 && count !== 8) return null;
  const codes: string[] = [];
  for (const match of value.matches) {
    if (!isJsonObject(match) || typeof match.boardCode !== 'string') return null;
    codes.push(match.boardCode);
  }
  const initial = createTournament(names, codes, value.startedAt);
  if (!initial || value.matches.length !== initial.matches.length) return null;
  const matches: TournamentMatch[] = [];
  for (let index = 0; index < value.matches.length; index += 1) {
    const match = readTournamentMatch(value.matches[index], initial.matches[index]);
    if (!match) return null;
    matches.push(match);
  }
  if (!isTournamentProgressValid(matches, count)) return null;
  if (!isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.currentMatch) || value.currentMatch >= matches.length)
    return null;
  if (value.turn !== 0 && value.turn !== 1) return null;
  const phase = readTournamentPhase(value.phase);
  if (!phase) return null;
  if (value.champion !== null && !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.champion)) return null;
  const tournament: Tournament = {
    startedAt: value.startedAt,
    players,
    matches,
    currentMatch: value.currentMatch,
    turn: value.turn,
    phase,
    champion: value.champion,
  };
  return isTournamentPhaseValid(tournament) ? tournament : null;
}

import { parseBoardCode } from '../deck.ts';
import { ELAPSED_MAX_MS, MOVES_MAX } from '../game.ts';
import { hasExactKeys, isJsonObject, isNonnegativeSafeInteger } from '../saved-format.ts';
import { compareTournamentResults } from './tournament-progress.ts';
import type { TournamentMatch, TournamentResult } from './tournament.ts';

export function readTournamentMatch(
  value: unknown,
  expected: TournamentMatch | undefined,
): TournamentMatch | null {
  if (
    !expected ||
    !isJsonObject(value) ||
    !hasExactKeys(value, ['round', 'stage', 'boardCode', 'players', 'results', 'winner'])
  )
    return null;
  if (
    value.round !== expected.round ||
    value.stage !== expected.stage ||
    typeof value.boardCode !== 'string' ||
    value.boardCode !== expected.boardCode
  )
    return null;
  const code = parseBoardCode(value.boardCode);
  if (!code || !twoValues(value.players) || !twoValues(value.results)) return null;
  const firstSeed = value.players[0];
  const secondSeed = value.players[1];
  if (!isTournamentSeed(firstSeed) || !isTournamentSeed(secondSeed)) return null;
  if (
    expected.round === 1 &&
    (firstSeed !== expected.players[0] || secondSeed !== expected.players[1])
  )
    return null;
  const minimumMoves = code.size ** 2 / 2;
  const firstResult = readResult(value.results[0], minimumMoves);
  const secondResult = readResult(value.results[1], minimumMoves);
  if (firstResult === undefined || secondResult === undefined) return null;
  if (
    (firstSeed === null && firstResult !== null) ||
    (secondSeed === null && secondResult !== null) ||
    (firstResult && firstResult.seed !== firstSeed) ||
    (secondResult && secondResult.seed !== secondSeed)
  )
    return null;
  const results: readonly [TournamentResult | null, TournamentResult | null] = [
    firstResult,
    secondResult,
  ];
  const winner =
    firstResult && secondResult ? compareTournamentResults(firstResult, secondResult) : null;
  if (value.winner !== winner) return null;
  return {
    round: expected.round,
    stage: expected.stage,
    boardCode: expected.boardCode,
    players: [firstSeed, secondSeed],
    results,
    winner,
  };
}

function twoValues(value: unknown): value is [unknown, unknown] {
  return Array.isArray(value) && value.length === 2;
}

function isTournamentSeed(value: unknown): value is number | null {
  return value === null || (isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value) && value >= 1 && value <= 8);
}

function readResult(value: unknown, minimumMoves: number): TournamentResult | null | undefined {
  if (value === null) return null;
  if (!isJsonObject(value) || !hasExactKeys(value, ['seed', 'moves', 'elapsedMs']))
    return undefined;
  if (
    !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.seed) ||
    value.seed < 1 ||
    value.seed > 8 ||
    !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.moves) ||
    value.moves < minimumMoves ||
    value.moves > MOVES_MAX ||
    typeof value.elapsedMs !== 'number' ||
    !Number.isFinite(value.elapsedMs) ||
    value.elapsedMs < 0 ||
    value.elapsedMs > ELAPSED_MAX_MS
  )
    return undefined;
  return { seed: value.seed, moves: value.moves, elapsedMs: value.elapsedMs };
}

import type { Tournament, TournamentMatch, TournamentPhase } from './tournament.ts';

export function isTournamentProgressValid(
  matches: readonly TournamentMatch[],
  count: number,
): boolean {
  if (matches.length !== (count === 4 ? 3 : 7)) return false;
  const roundCount = count === 4 ? 2 : 3;
  for (let round = 2; round <= roundCount; round += 1) {
    const priorRound = matches.filter((match) => match.round === round - 1);
    const nextRound = matches.filter((match) => match.round === round);
    if (priorRound.length !== nextRound.length * 2) return false;
    const priorComplete = priorRound.every((match) => match.winner !== null);
    const assigned = nextRound.some((match) => match.players.some((seed) => seed !== null));
    if (!priorComplete && assigned) return false;
    if (!assigned) continue;
    if (!priorComplete) return false;
    for (let index = 0; index < nextRound.length; index += 1) {
      const first = priorRound[index * 2]?.winner ?? null;
      const second = priorRound[index * 2 + 1]?.winner ?? null;
      if (nextRound[index]?.players[0] !== first || nextRound[index]?.players[1] !== second)
        return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

export function isTournamentPhaseValid(tournament: Tournament): boolean {
  const match = tournament.matches[tournament.currentMatch];
  if (!match) return false;
  const sameRound = tournament.matches
    .map((item, index) => ({ item, index }))
    .filter(({ item }) => item.round === match.round);
  if (sameRound.some(({ item, index }) => index < tournament.currentMatch && item.winner === null))
    return false;
  if (sameRound.some(({ item, index }) => index > tournament.currentMatch && item.winner !== null))
    return false;
  const first = match.results[0];
  const second = match.results[1];
  if (tournament.phase === 'ready' || tournament.phase === 'playing') {
    return (
      match.winner === null &&
      (tournament.turn === 0
        ? first === null && second === null
        : first !== null && second === null) &&
      match.players[tournament.turn] !== null &&
      tournament.champion === null
    );
  }
  if (tournament.phase === 'turn-finished')
    return (
      tournament.turn === 0 && first !== null && second === null && tournament.champion === null
    );
  if (tournament.phase === 'match-finished')
    return (
      tournament.turn === 1 &&
      match.winner !== null &&
      first !== null &&
      second !== null &&
      tournament.champion === null
    );
  return (
    tournament.turn === 1 &&
    match.stage === 'Final' &&
    match.winner !== null &&
    tournament.champion === match.winner &&
    tournament.matches.every((item) => item.winner !== null)
  );
}

export function readTournamentPhase(value: unknown): TournamentPhase | null {
  if (
    value === 'ready' ||
    value === 'playing' ||
    value === 'turn-finished' ||
    value === 'match-finished' ||
    value === 'finished'
  )
    return value;
  return null;
}

import { decodeSnapshot } from '../snapshot.ts';
import { isJsonObject, hasExactKeys, parseJson } from '../saved-format.ts';
import { decodeTournament } from './tournament-validation.ts';
import type { GameState } from '../game.ts';
import type { Tournament } from './tournament.ts';

export { decodeTournament } from './tournament-validation.ts';

export type TournamentPayload =
  | { readonly kind: 'setup'; readonly playerCount: 4 | 8; readonly names: readonly string[] }
  | {
      readonly kind: 'tournament';
      readonly tournament: Tournament;
      readonly game: GameState | null;
    };

export function encodeTournamentJson(
  tournament: Tournament | null,
  playerCount: 4 | 8,
  names: readonly string[],
  gameSnapshot: string,
): string {
  if (!tournament) {
    return JSON.stringify(
      { version: 1, type: 'setup', playerCount, names: names.slice(0, playerCount) },
      null,
      2,
    );
  }
  const game = tournament.phase === 'playing' ? parseJson(gameSnapshot) : null;
  return JSON.stringify({ version: 1, type: 'tournament', tournament, game }, null, 2);
}

export function decodeTournamentJson(text: string): TournamentPayload | null {
  if (new TextEncoder().encode(text).byteLength > 65_536) return null;
  const value = parseJson(text);
  if (!isJsonObject(value) || value.version !== 1 || typeof value.type !== 'string') return null;
  if (value.type === 'setup') {
    if (!hasExactKeys(value, ['version', 'type', 'playerCount', 'names'])) return null;
    if (
      (value.playerCount !== 4 && value.playerCount !== 8) ||
      !stringArray(value.names, value.playerCount)
    )
      return null;
    return { kind: 'setup', playerCount: value.playerCount, names: value.names };
  }
  if (
    value.type !== 'tournament' ||
    !hasExactKeys(value, ['version', 'type', 'tournament', 'game'])
  )
    return null;
  const tournament = decodeTournament(value.tournament);
  if (!tournament) return null;
  if (value.game === null)
    return tournament.phase === 'playing' ? null : { kind: 'tournament', tournament, game: null };
  if (tournament.phase !== 'playing') return null;
  const game = decodeSnapshot(JSON.stringify(value.game));
  const match = tournament.matches[tournament.currentMatch];
  if (!game || !match || game.boardCode !== match.boardCode) return null;
  return { kind: 'tournament', tournament, game };
}

function stringArray(value: unknown, length: number): value is string[] {
  return (
    Array.isArray(value) &&
    value.length === length &&
    value.every((item) => typeof item === 'string')
  );
}

import { hasExactKeys, isJsonObject, parseJson } from '../saved-format.ts';
import { decodeTournament } from './tournament-format.ts';
import type { PreferenceStore } from '../session/storage.ts';
import type { Tournament } from './tournament.ts';

export const TOURNAMENT_STORAGE_KEY = 'np3:tournaments';
const STORAGE_VERSION = 3;

export interface TournamentHistoryRead {
  readonly tournaments: Tournament[];
  readonly available: boolean;
}

export function readTournamentHistory(store: PreferenceStore | null): TournamentHistoryRead {
  if (!store) return { tournaments: [], available: false };
  try {
    const text = store.getItem(TOURNAMENT_STORAGE_KEY);
    if (!text) return { tournaments: [], available: true };
    const value = parseJson(text);
    if (
      !isJsonObject(value) ||
      !hasExactKeys(value, ['v', 'items']) ||
      value.v !== STORAGE_VERSION ||
      !Array.isArray(value.items)
    )
      return { tournaments: [], available: true };
    const tournaments: Tournament[] = [];
    for (const item of value.items) {
      const tournament = decodeTournament(item);
      if (!tournament || tournament.phase !== 'finished')
        return { tournaments: [], available: true };
      tournaments.push(tournament);
    }
    return { tournaments: tournaments.slice(0, 10), available: true };
  } catch {
    return { tournaments: [], available: false };
  }
}

export function writeTournamentHistory(
  store: PreferenceStore | null,
  tournaments: readonly Tournament[],
): boolean {
  try {
    store?.setItem(
      TOURNAMENT_STORAGE_KEY,
      JSON.stringify({ v: STORAGE_VERSION, items: tournaments.slice(0, 10) }),
    );
    return store !== null;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}

import { useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { freshBoardCodes } from '../session/fresh-board.ts';
import { browserStore } from '../session/use-saved-preferences.ts';
import {
  activeTournamentMatch,
  beginTournamentTurn,
  createTournament,
  nextTournamentTurn,
  normalizePlayerName,
  playerNamesError,
  tournamentBoardSizes,
} from './tournament.ts';
import { nextTournamentMatch, recordTournamentResult } from './tournament-progress.ts';
import { decodeTournamentJson, encodeTournamentJson } from './tournament-format.ts';
import { readTournamentHistory, writeTournamentHistory } from './tournament-storage.ts';
import type { GameState } from '../game.ts';
import type { Tournament, TournamentMatch } from './tournament.ts';

export function useTournament() {
  const [store] = useState(browserStore);
  const [historyRead] = useState(() => readTournamentHistory(store));
  const [playerCount, setPlayerCount] = useState<4 | 8>(4);
  const [names, setNames] = useState<string[]>(() => Array<string>(8).fill(''));
  const [tournament, setTournament] = useState<Tournament | null>(null);
  const [past, setPast] = useState(historyRead.tournaments);
  const pastRef = useRef(past);
  const [json, setJson] = useState('');
  const [notice, setNotice] = useState('');
  const [storageNotice, setStorageNotice] = useState(
    historyRead.available ? '' : "Progress won't be saved on this device.",
  );

  function editName(index: number, value: string): void {
    setNames((current) => current.map((name, position) => (position === index ? value : name)));
  }

  function startTournament(): boolean {
    const acceptedNames = names.slice(0, playerCount).map(normalizePlayerName);
    const error = playerNamesError(acceptedNames);
    if (error) {
      setNotice(error);
      return false;
    }
    const codes = freshBoardCodes(tournamentBoardSizes(playerCount));
    const usedIds = new Set(pastRef.current.map((item) => item.startedAt));
    let startedAt = Date.now();
    while (usedIds.has(startedAt))
      startedAt = startedAt === Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER ? 0 : startedAt + 1;
    const next = createTournament(acceptedNames, codes, startedAt);
    if (!next) {
      setNotice('Unable to start tournament.');
      return false;
    }
    setTournament(next);
    setNotice('');
    return true;
  }

  function startTurn(): TournamentMatch | undefined {
    if (!tournament || tournament.phase !== 'ready') return undefined;
    const match = activeTournamentMatch(tournament);
    setTournament(beginTournamentTurn(tournament));
    return match;
  }

  function finishTurn(game: GameState): void {
    setTournament((current) =>
      current ? recordTournamentResult(current, game.moves, game.elapsedMs) : current,
    );
  }

  function nextTurn(): void {
    setTournament((current) => (current ? nextTournamentTurn(current) : current));
  }

  function nextMatch(): void {
    if (!tournament) return;
    const next = nextTournamentMatch(tournament);
    setTournament(next);
    if (next.phase === 'finished') remember(next);
  }

  function remember(finished: Tournament): void {
    if (pastRef.current.some((item) => item.startedAt === finished.startedAt)) return;
    const next = [finished, ...pastRef.current].slice(0, 10);
    pastRef.current = next;
    setPast(next);
    setStorageNotice(
      writeTournamentHistory(store, next) ? '' : "Progress won't be saved on this device.",
    );
  }

  function exportJson(gameSnapshot: string): void {
    setJson(encodeTournamentJson(tournament, playerCount, names, gameSnapshot));
    setNotice('');
  }

  function loadJson():
    | { readonly kind: 'setup' }
    | {
        readonly kind: 'tournament';
        readonly phase: Tournament['phase'];
        readonly game: GameState | null;
      }
    | null {
    const payload = decodeTournamentJson(json);
    if (!payload) {
      setNotice('Invalid tournament.');
      return null;
    }
    setNotice('');
    if (payload.kind === 'setup') {
      setPlayerCount(payload.playerCount);
      setNames([...payload.names, ...Array<string>(8 - payload.names.length).fill('')]);
      setTournament(null);
      return { kind: 'setup' };
    }
    setTournament(payload.tournament);
    if (payload.tournament.phase === 'finished') remember(payload.tournament);
    return { kind: 'tournament', phase: payload.tournament.phase, game: payload.game };
  }

  function leaveTournament(): void {
    setTournament(null);
    setNotice('');
  }

  return {
    playerCount,
    setPlayerCount: (value: number) => setPlayerCount(value === 8 ? 8 : 4),
    names,
    editName,
    tournament,
    past,
    json,
    setJson,
    notice,
    storageNotice,
    startTournament,
    startTurn,
    finishTurn,
    nextTurn,
    nextMatch,
    exportJson,
    loadJson,
    leaveTournament,
  };
}

import { useRef } from 'react';
import type { RefObject } from 'react';
import { Board } from '../board/Board.tsx';
import type { BoardFocus } from '../board/Board.tsx';
import { GameStatus } from '../status/GameStatus.tsx';
import { TournamentBracket } from './TournamentBracket.tsx';
import { tournamentPlayer, activeTournamentMatch } from './tournament.ts';
import type { Tournament } from './tournament.ts';
import type { Session } from '../session/session.ts';

interface TournamentCurrentProps {
  readonly tournament: Tournament;
  readonly session: Session;
  readonly actionButton: RefObject<HTMLButtonElement | null>;
  activate(index: number): void;
  startTurn(): void;
  nextTurn(): void;
  nextMatch(): void;
  leaveTournament(): void;
  onBack(): void;
}

export function TournamentCurrent({
  tournament,
  session,
  actionButton,
  activate,
  startTurn,
  nextTurn,
  nextMatch,
  leaveTournament,
  onBack,
}: TournamentCurrentProps) {
  const board = useRef<BoardFocus>(null);
  const match = activeTournamentMatch(tournament);
  const playerSeed =
    tournament.phase === 'turn-finished'
      ? (match?.players[1] ?? null)
      : (match?.players[tournament.turn] ?? null);
  const player = tournamentPlayer(tournament, playerSeed);

  function runTournamentAction(): void {
    if (tournament.phase === 'playing') return;
    if (tournament.phase === 'ready') startTurn();
    else if (tournament.phase === 'turn-finished') nextTurn();
    else if (tournament.phase === 'match-finished') nextMatch();
    else onBack();
  }

  return (
    <section className="tournament-current">
      <div className="tournament-turn">
        <div
          className={
            tournament.phase === 'finished' ? 'tournament-champion' : 'tournament-turn-info'
          }
        >
          {tournament.phase === 'finished' ? (
            <h2>Champion: {tournamentPlayer(tournament, tournament.champion)?.name}</h2>
          ) : (
            <>
              {match && <p>Round: {match.stage}</p>}
              {player && tournament.phase !== 'match-finished' && (
                <h2>Now playing: {player.name}</h2>
              )}
            </>
          )}
        </div>
        <div className="tournament-actions">
          <button
            ref={actionButton}
            type="button"
            className="control"
            aria-disabled={tournament.phase === 'playing'}
            onClick={runTournamentAction}
          >
            {tournament.phase === 'ready'
              ? 'Start turn'
              : tournament.phase === 'playing'
                ? 'Turn in progress'
                : tournament.phase === 'turn-finished'
                  ? 'Next turn'
                  : tournament.phase === 'match-finished'
                    ? 'Next match'
                    : 'Back to game'}
          </button>
          {tournament.phase !== 'finished' && (
            <button type="button" className="control" onClick={leaveTournament}>
              Leave tournament
            </button>
          )}
        </div>
      </div>
      {tournament.phase === 'playing' && (
        <>
          <GameStatus
            game={session.game}
            best={undefined}
            celebration={session.celebration}
            showBest={false}
          />
          <p id="tournament-board-help" className="help">
            Use a pointer or Tab to enter the board. Arrow keys move between cards. Enter or Space
            reveals a card.
          </p>
          <div className="game-result">
            <p role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
              <span key={session.announcement}>{session.feedback}</span>
            </p>
          </div>
          <Board
            key={session.generation}
            game={session.game}
            helpId="tournament-board-help"
            activate={activate}
            ref={board}
          />
        </>
      )}
      <TournamentBracket tournament={tournament} />
    </section>
  );
}

import { useEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import { isWon } from '../game.ts';
import { SelectionKind } from '../selection.ts';
import { CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS, createClock, elapsedStep } from './browser-clock.ts';
import { tickSession } from './session.ts';
import type { RefObject } from 'react';
import type { Session } from './session.ts';

export function useSessionClock(
  session: Session,
  current: RefObject<Session>,
  commit: (next: Session) => void,
  enabled = true,
) {
  const clock = useRef(createClock(performance.now()));
  const visible = useRef(!document.hidden);
  const won = isWon(session.game);

  function running(): boolean {
    return (
      visible.current &&
      enabled &&
      !current.current.paused &&
      current.current.game.started &&
      !isWon(current.current.game)
    );
  }

  function synchronize(generation = current.current.generation): void {
    if (generation !== current.current.generation) return;
    const now = performance.now();
    const step = elapsedStep(clock.current, now, running());
    clock.current = step.clock;
    if (step.milliseconds) commit(tickSession(current.current, generation, step.milliseconds));
  }

  useEffect(() => {
    const generation = session.generation;
    let active = true;
    let timer: number | undefined;
    function schedule(): void {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      if (!active || generation !== current.current.generation || !running()) return;
      const selection = current.current.game.selection;
      const delay =
        selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch
          ? Math.min(CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS, selection.remainingMs)
          : CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS;
      timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        if (!active) return;
        synchronize(generation);
        schedule();
      }, delay);
    }
    function visibilityChanged(): void {
      if (!active || generation !== current.current.generation) return;
      synchronize(generation);
      visible.current = !document.hidden;
      schedule();
    }
    schedule();
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilityChanged);
    return () => {
      active = false;
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilityChanged);
    };
  }, [enabled, session.generation, session.game.started, session.paused, won]);

  useEffect(() => {
    clock.current = createClock(performance.now());
  }, [enabled]);

  return {
    synchronize,
    reset: () => {
      clock.current = createClock(performance.now());
    },
  };
}

import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { Board } from './board/Board.tsx';
import { Controls } from './controls/Controls.tsx';
import { Reproduction } from './controls/Reproduction.tsx';
import { GameStatus } from './status/GameStatus.tsx';
import type { BoardFocus } from './board/Board.tsx';
import { useGame } from './session/use-game.ts';
import { TournamentScreen } from './competition/Tournament.tsx';
import './game.css';

export function Game() {
  const [screen, setScreen] = useState<'game' | 'tournament'>('game');
  const controller = useGame({ clockActive: screen === 'game' });
  const { session } = controller;
  const { game } = session;
  const board = useRef<BoardFocus>(null);
  const tournamentButton = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);
  const tournamentHeading = useRef<HTMLHeadingElement>(null);
  const returnFocus = useRef(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (screen === 'tournament') tournamentHeading.current?.focus();
    else if (returnFocus.current) {
      returnFocus.current = false;
      tournamentButton.current?.focus();
    }
  }, [screen]);
  function resume(): void {
    board.current?.focusRemembered();
    controller.resume();
  }
  function openTournament(): void {
    controller.synchronize();
    setScreen('tournament');
  }
  function backToGame(): void {
    returnFocus.current = true;
    setScreen('game');
  }
  return (
    <main>
      <header>
        <p className="eyebrow">A little focus. A perfect pair.</p>
        <h1>Neon Pairs</h1>
      </header>
      <section hidden={screen !== 'game'}>
        <p className="intro">Reveal two cards. Match their shape and marker to keep the pair.</p>
        <Controls
          size={game.size}
          newGame={controller.newGame}
          restart={controller.restart}
          openTournament={openTournament}
          tournamentButtonRef={tournamentButton}
        />
        <GameStatus
          game={game}
          best={session.preferences.bestMoves[String(game.size)]}
          celebration={session.celebration}
        />
        <p id="board-help" className="help">
          Use a pointer or Tab to enter the board. Arrow keys move between cards. Enter or Space
          reveals a card.
        </p>
        <div className="game-result">
          <p role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
            <span key={session.announcement}>{session.feedback}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <Board key={session.generation} game={game} activate={controller.activate} ref={board} />
        <Reproduction
          game={game}
          generation={session.generation}
          exportSnapshot={controller.exportSnapshot}
          loadBoard={controller.loadBoard}
          loadSnapshot={controller.loadSnapshot}
          notice={session.loadNotice}
          paused={session.paused}
          resume={resume}
        />
      </section>
      {screen === 'tournament' && (
        <TournamentScreen onBack={backToGame} headingRef={tournamentHeading} />
      )}
    </main>
  );
}

import { useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { createGame } from '../game.ts';
import { parseBoardCode, isValidSize } from '../deck.ts';
import { decodeSnapshot, encodeSnapshot } from '../snapshot.ts';
import { freshBoardCode } from './fresh-board.ts';
import { activateSession, initialSession, replaceGame, SessionNotice } from './session.ts';
import { readPreferences } from './storage.ts';
import { browserStore, useSavedPreferences } from './use-saved-preferences.ts';
import { useSessionClock } from './use-session-clock.ts';
import type { Session } from './session.ts';
import type { GameState } from '../game.ts';

export function useGame(
  options: { readonly savePreferences?: boolean; readonly clockActive?: boolean } = {},
) {
  const [store] = useState(browserStore);
  const [session, setSession] = useState(() => {
    const preferences = readPreferences(store);
    return initialSession(freshBoardCode(preferences.size), preferences);
  });
  const current = useRef(session);

  function commit(next: Session): void {
    if (next === current.current) return;
    current.current = next;
    setSession(next);
  }

  const clock = useSessionClock(session, current, commit, options.clockActive ?? true);
  useSavedPreferences(store, session.preferences, options.savePreferences ?? true);

  function newGame(size = current.current.game.size): void {
    if (!isValidSize(size)) return;
    const next = createGame(freshBoardCode(size, current.current.game.seed));
    clock.reset();
    commit(replaceGame(current.current, next, false));
  }

  function restart(): void {
    clock.reset();
    commit(replaceGame(current.current, createGame(current.current.game.boardCode), false));
  }

  function notice(feedback: string): void {
    commit({
      ...current.current,
      feedback,
      loadNotice: feedback,
      announcement: current.current.announcement + 1,
    });
  }

  function loadBoard(code: string): boolean {
    code = code.trim();
    if (!parseBoardCode(code)) {
      notice(SessionNotice.invalidBoard);
      return false;
    }
    clock.reset();
    commit(replaceGame(current.current, createGame(code), false));
    return true;
  }

  function loadSnapshot(text: string): boolean {
    const game = decodeSnapshot(text);
    if (!game) {
      notice(SessionNotice.invalidSnapshot);
      return false;
    }
    clock.reset();
    commit(replaceGame(current.current, game, true));
    return true;
  }

  function restoreTournamentGame(game: GameState): void {
    clock.reset();
    commit(replaceGame(current.current, game, false));
  }

  function exportSnapshot(): string {
    // Rendered state can trail the active clock by a tick.
    clock.synchronize();
    return encodeSnapshot(current.current.game);
  }

  function activate(index: number): void {
    clock.synchronize();
    commit(activateSession(current.current, index));
  }

  function resume(): void {
    clock.reset();
    commit({
      ...current.current,
      paused: false,
      feedback: '',
      loadNotice: '',
    });
  }

  return {
    session,
    newGame,
    restart,
    loadBoard,
    loadSnapshot,
    restoreTournamentGame,
    exportSnapshot,
    activate,
    resume,
    synchronize: clock.synchronize,
  };
}
